Lambda Functions are deployed to an aws_lambda_function resource, but the most important
thing to set up first is the IAM role you will use for your Lambda Function. This will be how we
allow our Lambda Function access to other resources on AWS, such as secrets and logging. It is also
how we allow it to communicate with databases and other services our application code needs to
communicate with:
data "aws_iam_policy_document" "lambda" {
statement {
effect = "Allow"
